A||||16||Oreif||Q's of Exhaust for 1FST2M6||||5||
Z||000000||Oreif||11-15-2000||11:11 AM||||Right now I have the Sprint manifolds on my car with the stock exhaust. At present I was going to remove the Cat and go with Ocelot but from the other thread I see it's not the performance increase I thought. My questions are:<BR>Will removing the Cat help? (my car is exempt from Emission testing)<BR>What size pipe is too big? I see your going to 2.5" is 3" too big for a non-turbo?<BR>I saw an exhaust system that the person just had a 2 Cats but no muffler. (true dual, no Y-pipe) He said it was a huge performance gain and it was only excessively loud at WOT. Does this sound right or is he "blowing smoke"?<BR>What is the cost of the exhaust your installing soon?<BR>Thanks for any help. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-15-2000||11:43 AM||||the muffler i had installed just this morning was $139 for the muffler (retail) and $100 installed stainless 2.5" piping. $55 stainless tip. 3" piping has to be oval tubing so it won't scrape (2.26hx4.1w) (at least on my car) taking the cat off will make your car have less torque about 4lbft at the wheels. dual exhust will be better than stock but not good for torque. torque is what pushes you back in the seat HP keeps you going. Tq in my opinion is WAY more important.  the duals don't have to be really loud. <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>  and get thier free catalog and look at their "spin tech" mufflers. they are kinda small and not annoying in the car.  3" would propbly be a bit large. but if you have Nitrous you'd be ok. the sprint manifolds i have no experiance with so i can't help ya there. if you are really looking at duals try and have the fabricator install a balance tube from the front and rear banks this will increase torque a little and mellow out the sound so it's not so punchy. DON'T use "glas packs" they will have to be replaced in 4 months. use a welded baffle or if your dead set on a "glas pack" use somthing from Remus, Brullen, or Powertone they have a stainless mesh on the inside to help keep the fiberglas in the can. Dynomax also does this. a set of Dynomax XR-1s would be nice! 2.25 if your going dual. if you road race the car, upper RPM HP is great with duals. if your drag racing the car single in single out 2.5. those are what we have found to be the best yet. msweldon has true dual and isn't happy with it on his (basicly) stock 2.8. the 3.4TDC will have a 3"in dual 2.5 out brullen. he "has to have dual tips" his personal preferance. but you can't get good flow in a cross-flow design muffler and that hinders the scavaging effect/theory. a little back pressure is good.. to much is bad (pollute the combustion chamber with unburn fuel and already heated gases, glowing manifolds) and so is to little (glowing manifolds, burnt valves and no get up and go off idle).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> hope i haven't confused you.. what do you MOSTLY do with the car. high speed runs on the hwy and road racing (eg. slalom or closed course) or stop light bashing, ricer pickin on? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-15-2000||12:08 PM||||Usually it's just cruising down the highway with an occasional stop light to stop light race. I'm not looking to squeeze 600 hp out of my basically stock 2.8 but I don't want to spend a lot of money on minimal gains. I don't want to lose torque so I will buy a new cat (suspect mine is going). From what I have been told someone previously dyno'd the sprint manifolds and they offer the same gain as porting the stock manifolds. (if I knew then what I know now I probably would have bought real headers) I am not going to use glass packs. I want the exhaust to sound close to stock (loudness) but offer performance gains. It looks like I'll be doing the 2.5". Would I loose anything by going to a single in/single out 2.5 muffler but splitting the single out to keep the dual look?<BR>Thanks for the info||||reg||1
Z||000003||fotofrank||11-15-2000||01:27 PM||||Oreif,It just so happens I have a stock 2.5(used) muffler and a Dynomax turbo muffler in my garage. BTW how did you get exempt from emission testing?||||reg||10
Z||000004||msweldon||11-15-2000||01:43 PM||||Actually Trav,<P>As per your advice, 1FST, I'm going to stay with a single exhaust system on the TDC, using the stock TDC manifolds and maybe two of the small Brullen-glasspacks or two flowmaster race mufflers if I can pass emissions w/out a cat.<P>But yes, oreiF, the dual exhaust system I have on my stock 2.8 with glasspacks sounds really nice, and rev's "very" freely, but there is a noticable loss of torque down low.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||11-15-2000||01:44 PM||||Frank, How much for the Dynomax? As for exempt, I registered my car with my insurance company as a classic. Classic (not daily driven) and showcars are exempt from emission testing. You still get the notice every 2 years and you need to fill out a form (available at the testing station) and supply a copy of your insurance as proof. (every 2 years) Classic cars per my insurance company (Nationwide) are insured for appraised value and allowed 3500 miles per year. The cost of insurance is less because it is driven less.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||11-15-2000||02:11 PM||||YEAH! you can split the exhaust x2 out the single in/out  that will give you the look you want the the performance your looking for too. i'd jump all over that Dynomax! I just picked up my car about an hour ago and it's NICE AND QUIET! untill you stand on it and it's LOUD as H$LL!! pulls nice from 3000-redline. raced my friends miata.. and before i could pull him now i can pull him and sound nice doing it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><BR>that splitting the single out with a Y-pipe might not be a bad idea Marc! i'll call grand-muffler and the shop and see what they have on the shelf... for a 2.5"-180* in 4" hmm... might have to make that! i'll ask though. <P>you'll be very happy with the Dynomax! and Catco and Random Technologies make nice cats. but they ARE NOT good for nitrous application.. all the lierature says they are.. they are full of crap! i want through 16+ bottles and my cat was COMPLETELY empty!!! a $350 cat was GONE! so i put a straigh pipe on it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> the resonance of the empty cat (expansion chamber) was annoying. <P>------------------<BR>WOW... i've made chicken salad!!!||||reg||1
